---
/**
 * A user-state page. Everything on it comes out of the reader's own browser and
 * none of it exists at build time, so it carries noindex, is excluded from the
 * sitemap, and is deliberately NOT disallowed in robots.txt — a blocked path is
 * never fetched, so the tag would never be read.
 *
 * `client:only` for the same reason: SSR-ing an empty plan is a layout shift
 * for markup nobody reads.
 */
import PlanPage from '../components/plan/PlanPage.svelte';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Plan — eXir" description="Plan an occasion and get the shopping list that follows from it." noindex current="plan">
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Plan</h1>
    <p class="lede">What to make, how much of it, and what to buy — worked out from the drinks rather than guessed.</p>
  </section>

  {/* The island renders nothing until it hydrates, so its slot is zero-high
      and everything below it — the footer, the explanatory prose — starts at
      the top of the page and drops into place a moment later. That is a
      layout shift of almost half a viewport, measured, and it is the cost of
      `client:only` rather than an argument against it: none of this page is
      true at build time, so there is nothing honest to server-render.

      The space is reserved instead, the same way the navigation count reserves
      two digits before it knows the number. The placeholder is real markup so
      the area is not blank while the module arrives, and the island removes it
      on mount. */}
  <div class="tool-shell">
    <p class="wrap aside" data-tool-placeholder>Reading your plan…</p>
    <PlanPage client:only="svelte" />
  </div>

  <div class="wrap prose-page">
    <p>
      Nothing on this page leaves your browser. There are no accounts here and nothing to sign in
      to, which also means what you save lives in one browser on one device and the site cannot
      move it for you.
    </p>
    <p>
      A plan holds references, never figures. Every quantity above is recomputed from the drinks as
      they are today, so a plan saved a month ago quietly gains every correction made since. The
      link you can copy carries the same references and nothing else — not what you already have at
      home, and not the list itself.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
